; sample.key
;
; The keyfile may exist of lines starting with ';' or empty lines.
; There also must be eight keys in it, each key on it's own line.
;
; The keys must consist of 16 hexadecimal characters; 0..9 and A..F
;
; DES itself ignores the lowest bit of each byte, but Odette also derives its
; 2048-bit whitening from all 64 bits of every key, so every bit counts.
; Use random keys.

BA7CDE4350091ADE Leave at least one white space between the key
7F6644780026ADEF and any comment
CBDFE44672998390
BC7DEDACDBCFDDDE
00018849949F7367
BBFCDD6A88D3C000
3D91A7E20BC4F586
E8052B6C94F1D37A

After Odette has read the eight keys, it doesn't matter what else is in
the keyfile.
